course: dictionary
lesson: 8757
title: Seven: a number with more than one job
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Seven is a number. It is 7, one more than six and one less than eight. «A horse chestnut leaf is made of five to seven leaflets» means the leaf has between five and seven little leaves, so seven is how many.
explain: The words around seven give you clues about what it means. In «seven days», seven means the number of days in a week. In «seven o'clock», seven is a time on the clock. The clues tell you which meaning fits.
explain: A good check is to swap in the number 7 and see if the sentence still makes sense. In «Admiral Zheng He led seven great voyages», seven counts the voyages, so it is a number, not a time.
fact: Seven is the number 7, one more than six and one less than eight.
fact: A week is 7 days, so «seven days» means one week.
fact: «Seven o'clock» is a time on the clock.
fact: Seven is an odd number and a prime number, because only 1 and 7 divide it exactly.
fact: Ukrainian has seven cases, and «Мамо!» uses the vocative case, which is the case for calling someone.
exercise: «The land is split into continents, but how many depends on who is counting: seven in Britain and America.» How many continents does Britain count? | Five | Eight | Six | *Seven
exercise: «Seven o'clock» is a time on the clock. What does seven mean in «seven o'clock»? | A colour of the rainbow | *A time on the clock | A week of days | A number of things
exercise: Which number is one less than eight? | Ten | Six | *Seven | Nine
test: «Admiral Zheng He led seven great voyages from 1405 to 1433.» What does seven mean here? | *A number, counting how many voyages | A seven-year-old child | A time of day | A week of days
test: Is seven an odd number or an even number? | Both | Neither | *Odd | Even
exam: «A horse chestnut leaf is made of five to seven leaflets.» What is the most leaflets a leaf can have here? | Six | *Seven | Five | Eight
